# What a module behind the hop needs to check an admission: the public half of
# the hop's signing key. Public by design — a verifier must be able to hold it —
# so it is committed here with the playground's other local values.
#
# It is NOT generated, and that is the open half of security review r164 B1.
# `codefly config generate hop-signing SEED --service authority/hop` makes the
# hop's seed and keeps it inside Codefly; nothing derives the public half from
# it, so this value is written by hand for the playground and the two can drift
# silently (a wrong key refuses every call as stamp_proof). The sound producer
# is the authority publishing the hop's admission key through its own Keys path,
# which the verifier already trusts and already caches — an interfaces/authority
# change, proposed in the handbook before it is built.
#
# Until then: after generating the seed, derive its public half and set this key.
# libraries/hop/README.md, "Delivering the verification key", has the one
# command. The reservations are no longer configured here at all: they live in
# the console's own store (modules/console/services/store).
PUBLIC_KEY=
